697:## 2026-09-18T19:03:29-04:00 — **summariser refused: "approvals … differ from the bytes committed at 2642e4e"** (`oriented_cyl_2026-09-18_19:00:57_summarize_haa.log`). Cause: `verify_job` re-runs the finalizer's `verify_child` → `haa_approvals(closure, run_type, commit=<child's reviewed commit>)` → `exp06_profiles.load_approved_digests(path, repo, commit)`, which binds the CURRENT working-tree approvals bytes to the blob at the child's commit; `refill3` (c8611fc, compare/eval_launch for the sim path) changed the file after the children ran, so every HAA child now fails re-verification although nothing about the HAA keys changed. This is a design gap of the F3 wiring (re-verification of a historical child should read the approvals blob at the child's commit, not the working file) → **open should-fix for a follow-up round** (`tools/exp06_finalize.py::haa_approvals` / the summariser's re-verification), not fixable now without changing `finalize`. **Workaround, legitimate and documented:** the children's reviewed commits are 2642e4e, 8ce27e7, 9538479, 9ff4b3e, b0bae26, d45469c, 2e43887 — the approvals blob at every one of them is byte-identical to 8ed7684's (the version in force during the HAA runs; it approves the same summarize_haa 3f497fc4…, haa_* keys, gate_g1 and reused identities). After the sim queue exits: (1) ping "GPU 1 released"; (2) run the H3 comparer with the current file and `--approved-commit c8611fc`; (3) restore the working-tree approvals to 8ed7684's bytes (`git show 8ed7684:<path> > <path>`), run the summariser with `--approved-commit 2e43887` (its own gate: file == blob at that commit; producer digest equal), then `git checkout HEAD -- <path>`; every producer thus reads approvals identical to a reviewed committed version. Not doing it concurrently with the sim launchers, which bind the c8611fc version.
